From 6b3ad682efa3df4bd5a79185e7560280e3c3a676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:23:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shader): speculate descriptor table pointers and words
 with a runtime check

A T# or S# whose table pointer, or one of whose words, reaches its use
as a phi with an arm the SRT walker cannot evaluate (a lane mask, a
ballot, a route that never reaches the use) is refused with "is not a
valid runtime value", even when every path that does reach it carries
the same user-data pointer or the same loaded word.

With APS5_SPECULATE_DESCRIPTORS set, such a refusal prepares the program
again with DescriptorPointerSpeculation before the SRT walker: the
pointer is guessed from its only user-data leaf (the high half from the
next user-data register, else 0), and a word from its only load at a
constant offset (re-issued before the descriptor when the original does
not dominate it). The descriptor is built from the guess, and the shader
raises DescriptorFault at the load when the value it computes differs,
so a wrong guess is reported rather than silent. Off by default:
per-lane pointers selected in waterfall loops are not told apart from
stale arms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
